**Source offer (GPL section 6).** BtbN distributes prebuilt binaries only;
the obligation to make corresponding source available falls on this project
as the distributor of the built binary, not on BtbN. The corresponding source
for the binaries above is:

- FFmpeg at git commit `1005b294ff` on the `release/8.1` branch - the commit
  the `n8.1.2-53-g1005b294ff` version string names. Snapshot:
  `https://git.ffmpeg.org/gitweb/ffmpeg.git/snapshot/1005b294ff.tar.gz`
  (equivalently `https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/archive/1005b294ff.tar.gz`).
  This is NOT the `ffmpeg-8.1.tar.xz` release tarball; a snapshot 53 commits
  later is a different work and only the actual commit satisfies section 6.
- x264 at the commit BtbN's GPL build for this autobuild embedded. BtbN pulls
  x264's `stable` branch at build time and does not publish that commit in
  the release metadata; the shipped `libavcodec.so` reports it in its build
  configuration string, readable with
  `strings libavcodec.so | grep -o 'x264 [0-9]*'` and
  `ffmpeg -version` against the bundled libraries.

Anyone who receives the Linux binary of Infinite may request this exact
corresponding source under GPLv2-or-later/GPLv3 section 6. The written offer
is: open an issue at the project's repository.

**Release blocker, not yet done.** Section 6 is satisfied by an offer that is
good for three years and actually fulfillable. Before the Linux binary is
distributed, the release process must (a) download the FFmpeg snapshot above
and the matching x264 source, (b) record their SHA256 sums here so a recipient
can verify what they got, and (c) archive both tarballs as release assets
alongside the AppImage so fulfilment does not depend on upstream URLs staying
up. Until (a)-(c) are done, this file names a commit but does not yet pin a
verified source archive.

**Licence texts shipped with the Linux build.** `LICENSE.txt` inside each
