`u2netp.onnx` on Windows.

x264 (Linux, `INFINITE_ENABLE_GPL_CODECS=ON` only)
---------------------------------------------------

The H.264 encoder FFmpeg's `libavcodec` uses for `Platform::RecorderStart`'s
video track when GPL codecs are enabled. Not linked directly by Infinite -
it is compiled into the BtbN FFmpeg build's `libavcodec.so` - but it is the
component that makes the resulting binary GPL rather than merely
LGPL-encumbered, and the reason the Linux build is a first-time H.264
encoder *distributor* for this project (see `LICENSE` and
`docs/plans/linux/phase-03-media.md`).

Licence: GNU General Public License v2 or later. Source pinned above
alongside FFmpeg's. Licence text: `third_party/x264/COPYING`.

VA-API hardware encode
-----------------------

Not used. Considered as a way to move Linux's H.264 encoding burden onto
GPU-vendor-licensed silicon (matching macOS's VideoToolbox and Windows'
Media Foundation hardware paths) but explicitly scoped out of Phase 3 - it
cannot be verified under the llvmpipe container or in CI, and is deferred to
a phase with real hardware. libx264 software encode is the only Linux H.264
path today.

Signalsmith Stretch (all platforms)
-----------------------------------

Time-stretch / pitch-shift for Arrangement Timeline audio Samples
(`src/audio/dsp/ClipTimeStretch.h`). Header-only, vendored in
`external/signalsmith-stretch/`.

| Component | Version | Commit |
|---|---|---|
| signalsmith-stretch | 1.3.2 | `57b93f4e9206a089a45387eaa39bdc9f310d3308` |
| signalsmith-linear | 0.3.1 | `5668673560146a9cfe38c25315071e3fd68c8317` |

Local modifications (marked `INFINITE PATCH`):
- `signalsmith-stretch.h`: the silent-input bypass also waits until the
  output latency's worth of silence has been produced, so synthesis tails are
  not cut off at stretch rates above about 2x.
- `signalsmith-linear/fft.h`: adds the missing `#include <cstring>`
  (`std::memcpy`); it built only through libc++'s transitive includes and
  fails on libstdc++ (Linux) and MSVC.

FFT backend: Apple's Accelerate on macOS; the library's built-in portable
C++ FFT on Windows and Linux (no intrinsics, so x64 and ARM64 alike).
Measured at the same cost and bit-identical output to the Accelerate path.

Licence: MIT. Licence texts: `external/signalsmith-stretch/LICENSE.txt` and
`external/signalsmith-stretch/signalsmith-linear/LICENSE.txt`.
